From: WFI-048 -- close the patch-applier and embedded-path bypasses
Subject: [PATCH] feat(guard): read the patch, and find a path inside a token

Human-applied patch. All nine targets are protected gate artifacts; the guard
refuses an agent write to every one of them, which is the whole point of this
change.

APPLY THIS PATCH WHOLE. The three guard twins validate the generated invariant
export set exactly, so the guards and the generated modules must move together.
Applying only part of it makes the guards fail to load their invariants, and a
load failure is a hard deny of every tool call -- fail-closed and very loud, but
a lockout until the rest is applied.

What it does:
  1. Patch appliers (git apply, git am, patch, including -R/--reverse and stdin
     redirection) now have their patch READ. Every path the diff declares in its
     --- and +++ headers is tested, so a staged patch that rewrites a protected
     file can no longer be applied by an agent. Unreadable or unparseable
     patches fail closed. Inspection flags (--check, --stat, --numstat,
     --summary, --dry-run) stay allowed: they modify nothing, and
     docs/ci-staging/README.md tells a human to run exactly that first.
  2. A protected path EMBEDDED in a larger token -- open('<path>','a') -- is now
     found. The existing end-anchored test runs first and is unchanged, so this
     can only add denials.
  3. Four new generated invariants carry the patch-applier vocabulary and the
     boundary character class, so all four runtime modules derive them from
     guard-invariants.json. The generator remains the authority.

Not closed, and recorded rather than counted as covered: `python3 <script>`,
where the script decides its targets at runtime. Undecidable in general.

See docs/workflow-improvements/WFI-048.md.

Verify, then apply:
    git apply --check reports/notes/wfi-048a-guard-patch-target-and-embedded-path.patch
    git apply reports/notes/wfi-048a-guard-patch-target-and-embedded-path.patch
    python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/generate-guard-invariants.py --check

